  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the campaign for the autonomy of the indigenous people of Roraima</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIR is an organisation that was created to campaign for the demarcation of Indigenous territories in Roraima.  This demarcation was approved in 2005 but there still remain many challenges in ensuring that Indigenous communities in this area are able to live sustainably, including food security, ethno-development and health, in addition to ensuring that the demarcation of territory is respected. CIR helps organisations to fight against invasion of their land and protect their territory, helps with community projects, judicial accompaniment and communications and awareness raising among other work.  CIR works with 224 communites from different tribes (Makuxi, Wapichana, Ingarik&#xf3;, Taurepang, Patamona e Wai Wai) which amounts to around 30,000 indigenous people in 8 regions.  Our support aims to help CIR strengthen its capacity as an organisation so that it is better able to support the work of the communities through:
1) Increase the capacity of CIR to produce project proposals
2) Strengthen the relationship and communication between CIR and indigenous movements at the local level.</narrative>
  </description>
